-- title:
--   Commuting With GComplete Of Com Main And Self Consistency
-- statement:
--   **Commuting with the complete part follows from commutativity and self-consistency.**
--
--   Let `params` be LIDT parameters, `strategy` a symmetric successor strategy, and `family` a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family. Let $\gamma$ and $\zeta$ satisfy the stated nonnegativity and boundedness assumptions, and assume `hcom` gives `ComMainConclusion` while `hself` gives complete-part self-consistency. The resulting package is `CommutingWithGCompleteStatement`; its nontrivial error is
--
--   $$
--   36m\left(\gamma^{1/16}+\zeta^{1/16}+\left(\frac{d}{q}\right)^{1/16}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The theorem supplies the ordered-versus-reversed complete products, point-versus-complete products, and total complete-part products. It is used by `gHatFacts` and by the downstream theorem that starts from `ComMainConclusion` and self-consistency.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commutingWithGComplete_ofComMainAndSelfConsistency`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
